course: dictionary
lesson: 12706
title: Domesticated: tamed for people
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words describe things that people have changed over a long time. Domesticated is one of them. Look at the clues: «The farmer's domesticated cows graze in the field.» Cows do not live wild on their own. People have tamed and bred them, so domesticated means tamed and bred by people.
explain: The history can give you clues too. «Early farmers domesticated wild grasses into wheat.» Wild grass did not turn into wheat by itself. People chose and planted the best plants again and again, over many generations, until they were useful to us. Domesticate is the verb, and domesticated is its past form.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it in. «The farmer's tamed and bred cows graze in the field» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning. In a joke like «Sam has become very domesticated», the word means he now cooks and cleans, which is a different use for a person.
fact: Domesticated means tamed and bred by people over many generations, so that the animal or plant lives with us or is useful to us.
fact: Dogs, cows, sheep and wheat are domesticated. A wild wolf or wild grass is not.
fact: Domesticate is the verb, and domesticated is its past form: «Early farmers domesticated wolves into dogs.»
fact: A single tame animal is not the same as a domesticated one. A tamed lion has been tamed, but its kind was not bred by people for generations.
fact: As a joke, «domesticated» can describe a person who likes or is good at housework and cooking.
exercise: «The farmer's domesticated cows graze in the field.» What does domesticated mean? | Wild and free in the forest | *Tamed and bred by people over many generations | Very large and noisy | Hungry and thin
exercise: «Early farmers domesticated wild grasses into wheat.» What did the farmers do to the grasses? | *Tamed and bred them so they were useful to people | Chopped them down for firewood | Let them grow wild | Painted them green
exercise: Which of these is a domesticated animal? | *A sheep on a farm | A shark in the sea | A fox in the woods | A wild wolf in the mountains
test: «Dogs were domesticated from wolves thousands of years ago.» Find and copy one word that is the past form of the verb domesticate. | *domesticated | dogs | wolves | years
test: Mum says, «Ben has become very domesticated since he moved into his flat.» What does she mean? | He has lost his keys | *He now cooks and cleans for himself | He is now a wild animal in the flat | He has bought a pet snake
exam: Which best explains the meaning of domesticated? | Very old and very tall | Only a lion can be domesticated | *Tamed and bred by people over many generations | Found in the wild, far away from people
